1. A display element drive method for a display element including a light-emitting unit, a drive transistor, and a capacitor coupled to a gate of the drive transistor, the method comprising:

applying a supply voltage to one of a source and a drain of the drive transistor, another of the source and the drain of the drive transistor being electrically connected to the light-emitting unit;

placing the gate of the drive transistor in a floating state;

while the gate is in the floating state, applying a ramp waveform signal to a terminal capacitively coupled to the gate, thereby varying a potential of the floating gate in accordance with a slope of the ramp waveform signal; and

after applying the ramp waveform signal, applying a predetermined constant voltage to the gate of the drive transistor,

wherein a voltage written to the capacitor is determined according to the slope of the ramp waveform signal, and the drive transistor drives the light-emitting unit based on the voltage written to the capacitor.
